      <h1 id="installing-mirroring-disconnected-about" class="group scroll-mt-20">About disconnected installation mirroring<a href="#installing-mirroring-disconnected-about" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">As a cluster administrator, you can use a mirror registry to ensure that your clusters only use container images that satisfy your organizational controls on external content.</p>
      <h2 id="installing-mirroring-disconnected-con_installing-mirroring-disconnected-about" class="group scroll-mt-20">Mirror registries for installing clusters in disconnected environments<a href="#installing-mirroring-disconnected-con_installing-mirroring-disconnected-about" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You must mirror required container images into a disconnected environment before you can install and provision a cluster there. To mirror those container images, you must have a mirror registry.</p>
      <p>Consider the following options for creating and using a mirror registry:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>If you already have a container image registry, such as Red Hat Quay, you can use it as your mirror registry. If you do not already have a registry, you must create one.</li>
      <li>After you establish your registry, you need mirroring tools. To mirror your OpenShift Container Platform image repository to the mirror registry in your disconnected environment, you can use the oc-mirror OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>) plugin. The oc-mirror plugin is a single tool that mirrors all required OpenShift Container Platform content and other images to your mirror registry. The oc-mirror plugin is the preferred method for mirroring.</li>
      <li>Alternately, you can use the <code>oc adm</code> command to mirror just release and catalog images for OpenShift Container Platform.</li>
      </ul>
